  "notes": "West leads the ♥6 against 4♠. East wins the first 2 heart tricks and gives West a heart ruff. West exits a diamond, won in dummy. South must hope to pick up the trump suit and squeeze West in diamonds and clubs.\n\nSouth's only chance is that West is 1156. If East has 3 or more diamonds, he will guard that suit and the squeeze will not function. If East has 3 or more clubs, South lacks the dummy entries to isolate the club threat and have an entry at the time of the squeeze.\n\nSince West must be 1156 for South to have a chance, South should take a first round trump finesse. South plays all but 1 of the trumps.\n\nOn the second last trump, a diamond discard from West gives up an immediate trick. A club discard will allow South to set up a club trick by ruffing. Dummy has a diamond entry to reach the winning club.",
